language ESSENCE' 1.0

$ 5x5 Minesweeper puzzle.
$
$ Initial board (? = hidden, . = revealed safe):
$
$   .  .  ?  ?  ?
$   .  .  ?  ?  ?
$   .  ?  ?  ?  ?
$   .  ?  ?  ?  ?
$   .  ?  ?  ?  ?
$
$ Hidden mines: (1,3) and (5,2)
$
$ Deduction: revealed cells in the top-left corner propagate via
$ neighbour-count constraints. The $#REVEAL mechanism fires each time
$ a safe cell is deduced, unlocking further constraints.

letting height be 5
letting width be 5

$ known[r,c]: true = revealed at start
letting known be [
    [true,  true,  false, false, false],
    [true,  true,  false, false, false],
    [true,  false, false, false, false],
    [true,  false, false, false, false],
    [true,  false, false, false, false]
]

$ mines[r,c]: the hidden ground truth
letting mines be [
    [false, false, true,  false, false],
    [false, false, false, false, false],
    [false, false, false, false, false],
    [false, false, false, false, false],
    [false, true,  false, false, false]
]
